       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.2, compiled on          3925 1451   27
       02-28-2014 10:42:45 AM at Petten, the, Netherlands. The RRR3925 1451   28
       expands from 0 to 2.781615E+5 eV, with resonance           3925 1451   29
       extracted from the "radiator" TARES database. A total of   3925 1451   30
       3 l-values are used and 335 resonances. The resonance      3925 1451   31
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              3925 1451   32
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       3925 1451   33
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          3925 1451   34
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     3925 1451   35
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    3925 1451   36
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  3925 1451   37
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   3925 1451   38
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          3925 1451   39
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       3925 1451   40
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    3925 1451   41
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       3925 1451   42
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         3925 1451   43
       The s-wave average level spacing is 3699 eV and            3925 1451   44
       the s-wave neutron strength is 4.653e-05 1e-4.             3925 1451   45
